// IRIW with a control dependency between each reader's two loads.
//
// rmm-zoo property: mca (Atomicity / Multicopy atomic).
// Source: Alglave et al., "Herding Cats" (TOPLAS 2014) -- the ctrl variants of
//         the IRIW family; Sarkar et al., PLDI 2011.
//
// A control dependency from a load to a later LOAD is not preserved by any of
// POWER, ARMv7 or ARMv8 (only ctrl+isb / ctrl+isync is), so this variant is
// allowed even on multicopy-atomic hardware. It is included as the negative
// control against IRIW+addrs.lit: the two differ only in the kind of dependency,
// and only the address dependency is architecturally ordering.
//
// Reference verdicts: POWER, ARMv7, ARMv8 ALLOW (ctrl to a load is not ordering).
//                     SC and x86-TSO FORBID.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  y := 1
} ||| {
  r1 := x;
  if (r1 = 1) {
    r2 := y
  } else {
    r2 := y
  }
} ||| {
  r3 := y;
  if (r3 = 1) {
    r4 := x
  } else {
    r4 := x
  }
}
%%
allow (r1 = 1 && r2 = 0 && r3 = 1 && r4 = 0) [Power]
